mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><span style="font-size: 18pt;">Dynamics and Roles in Different Phases of the Projec</span></span></b><b style="font-size: 1rem;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><span style="font-size: 18pt;">t</span></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><b style="font-size: 1rem;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB"><span style="font-size: 18pt;"><br></span></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">Be in control over the dynamics at every stage of your transdisciplinary
project. Jointly explore and define the problem, and work effectively on
solutions by collaborating strategically and sharing new insights with each
other. Discover below how you can optimize your team process and disseminate
results using the&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.inholland.nl/onderzoek/publicaties/the-co-design-canvas-2023-english/" style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Co-design
Canvas</a><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;"> (Smeenk, 2020).</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-filename="Schermafbeelding 2024-11-13 183740.jpg" style="width: 700.304px; height: 497.012px;"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB"><br></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">“<i>If we want the ideas of involved citizens to have an impact, it can
only be achieved through good collaboration with other parties</i>.”<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">Wina Smeenk, Professor of Societal Impact Design at Inholland
University of Applied Sciences.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB"><o:p><br></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">There are three phases in a transdisciplinary process:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana">1.<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif">Exploring
the Problem</span></b><span style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana">2.<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp; </span></span><!--[endif]--><b><span style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif">Defining
the Problem</span></b><span style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">3.<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;">&nbsp;
</span></span><!--[endif]--><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;
line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Solving
the Problem and Disseminating Results</span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:36.0pt;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l1 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Exploring Each Other and the Problem<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">In phase 1, you explore the collaboration with your team members and the
problem you are going to work on together (Oskam, 2023). You want to get to
know each other and learn more about the issue at hand.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">In short, you are looking to answer the following questions:</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB"><br></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB"><o:p></o:p></span></p><ul style="margin-top:0cm" type="disc">
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;
     line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Who
     are the problem owners?<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;
     line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Who
     is needed to implement the solutions?<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo2;
     tab-stops:list 36.0pt"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;
     line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Who
     will be affected by the potential solutions?<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:0cm;
margin-left:36.0pt"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;
font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">It's helpful to think broad. Consider including artists, animals, or
nature in your theme exploration. Take enough time to get to know each other
and clarify each other's expectations. A shared understanding of the problem is
most important.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">Getting to know your subject begins with identifying the different
perspectives on the issue. This helps you understand the impact of the problem
and define it more clearly. <o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Defining the Problem<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">Based on the insights from the previous phase, you now collectively
formulate the problem definition. Make sure this results in a shared definition,
not just from your own viewpoint or experiences. While brainstorming, focus on
what your understandings have in common rather than the differences.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Solving the Problem and Disseminating Results<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">In phase 3, you work on solutions and new insights on the problem. Be
aware that the results of your transdisciplinary project are not always easily
measurable. In some cases, it is possible to deliver concrete results, while in
others, the results may be less visible. Regularly reflect on the process and outcomes,
and celebrate interim results together.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:
14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:
EN-GB">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:14.0pt;line-height:116%;font-family:&quot;Verdana&quot;,sans-serif;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Practical Tool</span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0cm"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;">The&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.inholland.nl/inhollandcom/about-inholland/co-design-canvas/" style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">&nbsp;Co-design Canvas</a>&nbsp;<span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt;">by Smeenk (2023) can assist you in the starting phase
of the collaboration. It can help with consciously visualizing the collaboration
between team members on forehand, the way you are going to involve
stakeholders, structure and document the process, and the communication.</span></p>                                                                      </body></html>